[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122474"] :question/problem "Determine the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\,j\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\\,Q(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=0\\,⟹\\,x=y=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,(x,y)\\ne (0,0)}.\n$$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=0\\,⟹\\,y=\\pm x\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $Q$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y\\ne \\pm x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y\\ne \\pm x}\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-122660/selection/ba2ac5ee76bc68e8b8b8b2c561038dd69da42db5b7b9ba7ad083c9aeab43703c" :answer/id #uuid "4b6aca0e-c557-5f15-aa31-343047fba81f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4,\\,x\\ne 1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122660/selection/cdc28bf7c25ce66f8d8935d83720310b62c8b1fc18a984f7dc0e14efb0f0336d" :answer/id #uuid "e8036336-f315-5293-b75b-8fb505c40d85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122660/selection/46b3dad4d31125372120d8079202fef3c1dfe19ae1d4faf2d2914c8b54c184ed" :answer/id #uuid "ed746dc3-9f51-59f0-aead-0b4738bf53b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,x\\ne 1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122660/selection/e539e5e6d90409c944c0c16e257a2daf3330ce5ca07d38991ad5e275fdc72c95" :answer/id #uuid "13395398-ea67-55a6-a2fe-9a5f8f74f59e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122660/selection/6c2146ce522483bb0ffb591dfab9ccf0fbe911e329304b4a8ab8bdd99db1b872" :answer/id #uuid "382a6ac4-4b0c-548d-ade1-b2566d6843b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122660/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "72dd5def-6976-59bc-873c-3d8ebef8e768" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122660/selection/ba2ac5ee76bc68e8b8b8b2c561038dd69da42db5b7b9ba7ad083c9aeab43703c" :answer-field/choices ["q-122660/selection/ba2ac5ee76bc68e8b8b8b2c561038dd69da42db5b7b9ba7ad083c9aeab43703c" "q-122660/selection/cdc28bf7c25ce66f8d8935d83720310b62c8b1fc18a984f7dc0e14efb0f0336d" "q-122660/selection/46b3dad4d31125372120d8079202fef3c1dfe19ae1d4faf2d2914c8b54c184ed" "q-122660/selection/e539e5e6d90409c944c0c16e257a2daf3330ce5ca07d38991ad5e275fdc72c95" "q-122660/selection/6c2146ce522483bb0ffb591dfab9ccf0fbe911e329304b4a8ab8bdd99db1b872"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122660" :question/id #uuid "76ab55a5-b7ae-513b-bef2-54d7a5d78561" :question/math-academy-id "q-122660" :question/problem "Determine the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4})\\,i+\\frac{xy}{x-1}\\,j\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4}),\\,Q(x,y)=\\frac{xy}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4=0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}.\n$$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\nx-1=0\\,⟹\\,x=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $Q$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne 1}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4,\\,x\\ne 1}\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122660/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67b7ea90-38e0-54b5-b76e-816beb0d48f9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122660"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122685/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "3cdbaf85-3d8b-522f-a03c-d8c7458ce51c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122685/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a08b5f42-d6f8-51a1-a1c9-7d63d7fcbafd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122685/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "d948be7d-56a0-5268-9c7b-1b3dc5eb032a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122685/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "c9e35abc-3303-56bd-88a9-5caf5d89a794" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122685/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "96e8fbc6-2055-580e-971b-59c91acb8375" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122685/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "84ff913a-8f18-55e8-bafd-bb9c42d01c1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122685/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-122685/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-122685/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-122685/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-122685/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-122685/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122685" :question/id #uuid "086063e9-05eb-5d55-a741-bf5ec8233d7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122685" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $T(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k$\n- $U(t)=2t\\,i-{t}^{2}\\,j-\\sqrt{t}\\,k$\n- $V(x,y,z)={e}^{-2z}\\sqrt{x+y}$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $T(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}$ to a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $U(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122685/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122685"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122691/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f58579e1-38d4-5abf-a391-0e05562d5170" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122691/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "31345475-d75e-55ca-a077-85af4281c264" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122691/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "5f363fab-f09e-5c7e-ba5f-9a7e0de9d322" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122691/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "6092ce9c-b2fe-5009-a68b-85f3d536466f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122691/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "ab5def73-abcc-57c9-a2f1-cae201603545" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122691/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "194c90ba-8bf2-50fd-bd39-9c9544d43226" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122691/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-122691/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-122691/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-122691/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-122691/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-122691/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122691" :question/id #uuid "c6a5608a-0fba-5a52-ac34-08b868b05a8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-122691" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $U(x,y,z)=(x+2){e}^{yz}$\n- $V(x,y,z)=⟨5{e}^{-{z}^{2}},{x}^{3}y,1-{y}^{3}⟩$\n- $W(x,y)=⟨x-3{y}^{2},2-y⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $U(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $V(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}$ to a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $W(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122691/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122710/selection/2c3956251d491613aa3209cca25c001bc077d873222007fa4fd703bcacb6698e" :answer/id #uuid "d804cc89-6cb0-567a-8f85-fb68e8da8434" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/49000dd6905017bc64c9a67b6d8a2ea475a684477ac6e02d6ed15c4c7dbbb3aa.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122710/selection/0c7c4598072e4f92303b09d3353cdd73af67ed1981ab6fe8b62f265f52f62b7a" :answer/id #uuid "c2202c2e-575e-5ab0-91e3-25864435fc30" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/4aeebc183f9a6676f7487fce53ec46ad0f2cc91a87847d8a230471dc638ea448.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122710/selection/000a002365d234e3a0516fb6322bab030dad6c4bf43c12ecf2baafb99932c6d1" :answer/id #uuid "ea3adc76-c737-5032-855e-572384003f95" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/de222a9251e08861dd06fdee593cc10557f0be1d2c7d891395512d699b35aa63.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122710/selection/8175f85ff4a5fc9ab2e01d21be82c15d4be3365ef7caf3636936599cf608a060" :answer/id #uuid "bcb0f591-3ae4-5e91-84c5-3ad30e823fd4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/11cfd599bbfe85c9f3c7a23d5b95c6bd2b3ff199c6c0a4777429123afc74cb8c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122710/selection/5a713a8e4617920d10b2e4744a66a96a5750d322a448388f03d5a0ec20e9ebd6" :answer/id #uuid "85538cb8-1a09-5134-b35e-4ce3eb95bc55" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/ff0774689ae7215b624ea7eb3bed8f68a673fba4bcc4ceeb73f82b9081c32d4f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122710/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "13614c47-5b79-5bee-9be8-d11672cb5627" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122710/selection/2c3956251d491613aa3209cca25c001bc077d873222007fa4fd703bcacb6698e" :answer-field/choices ["q-122710/selection/2c3956251d491613aa3209cca25c001bc077d873222007fa4fd703bcacb6698e" "q-122710/selection/0c7c4598072e4f92303b09d3353cdd73af67ed1981ab6fe8b62f265f52f62b7a" "q-122710/selection/000a002365d234e3a0516fb6322bab030dad6c4bf43c12ecf2baafb99932c6d1" "q-122710/selection/8175f85ff4a5fc9ab2e01d21be82c15d4be3365ef7caf3636936599cf608a060" "q-122710/selection/5a713a8e4617920d10b2e4744a66a96a5750d322a448388f03d5a0ec20e9ebd6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122710" :question/id #uuid "2c6bc97f-7c2a-5b13-a87c-12910c19f149" :question/math-academy-id "q-122710" :question/problem "Determine which of the following shaded regions depicts the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-{x}^{2})\\,i+x\\sqrt{1-|y|}\\,j\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-{x}^{2}),\\,Q(x,y)=x\\sqrt{1-|y|}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined when the expression under the logarithm is positive. So, to find the domain, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n1-{x}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,-1<x<1.\n$$\n\nThis defines the region ${D}_{1},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/89c78ec587826c15c90ef4ffdfc0fd9f8af3d7b4d3d1cc099ce24b883b9842c2.png)\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined the expression under the radical is positive or equal to zero. So, to find the domain, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n1-|y|\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,-1\\le y\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThis defines the region ${D}_{2},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/addd649aa739711fd34ebd3e82579c8c0100a2b9a109d5cafabde750bc94eb9a.png)\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by ${D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2},$ shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/49000dd6905017bc64c9a67b6d8a2ea475a684477ac6e02d6ed15c4c7dbbb3aa.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122710/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67b7ea90-38e0-54b5-b76e-816beb0d48f9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122710"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
